  "_about": "the GIANT PANDA sculpted on the bear's rig scaled to 1.5 m (2026-11-06, round 2; gen: scratchpad sc/m5/giantpanda.py): a heavy white barrel, the rump round and high, on thick rounded black legs with broad paws; a broad black band over the shoulders and round the chest into the forelegs; a big ROUND white head -- big cheek masses, the forehead rising steeply from a short muzzle -- large black oval patches round the small eyes slanting down and out, big round black ears on top, a black nose; a short white tail. Slow and placid; lies down at its stops SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw (4 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): round black cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`); the roots faired.",
